<h3>Description</h3>
<p>NOT in TRSE is functionally equal to XOR or ^</p>
<p>Conditionals in TRSE does not support NOT, so be mindful of this. Ie


<code>
   if a = b then  // correct way of checking whether 'a' is equal to 'b'
   if a <> b then  // correct way of checking whether 'a' is not equal to 'b'
   if not a = b then  // will XOR 'a' before checking if the result is equal with 'b'
</code>
